{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice because Old Sock and Memphis connect with the blues mood I want to continue today.",
    "Different Shades Of Blue fits my interest in the guitar-led blues of People, Hell & Angels; the roots-and-soul and country-rooted choices also reflect parts of my recent listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shadows in the Night and Heaven & Earth miss my current mood because traditional pop standards and progressive rock do not give me the blues and roots-rock sound I want now.",
    "Popular Problems emphasizes lyric-focused songwriting when I am more interested in blues playing; reflective songwriting alone is not enough to make it a strong choice today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to stretch my interest in blues and roots rock into a broader interest in familiar rock and singer-songwriter albums.",
    "My interest in You Should Be So Lucky seems to carry too much weight as a reason to suggest reflective songwriting, even when the sound does not match my current mood."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The shared blues appeal of Old Sock, Memphis, and People, Hell & Angels matters more to me today than a loose connection to any one album in my history.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I would choose now: Play All Night appeals musically, but I would save a long live album for later and choose only my two strongest matches today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my broader roots-oriented taste, but only some capture the blues-focused listening mood that drives my choices today."
}"}
